9. FAILURE ANALYSIS
==================================================

Add the ability for a Producer Monitor card to answer:

"Why did a producer fail after stage=produced?"

Use the existing EntryProduceError as the authoritative trading-side failure model.

Existing structure:

type EntryProduceError struct {
    Code            EntryProduceErrorCode

    Producer        EntryProducer
    Side            string
    OrderID         string

    CleanupRequired bool

    Err error // optional runtime-specific diagnostic
}

Do NOT invent a separate unrelated BOT OPS failure interpretation.

Each producer helper constructs the authoritative EntryProduceError at the exact point where the failure becomes known.

Higher-level producer orchestration must not reinterpret, classify, or replace that failure.

produceEntry() (or the Producer Monitor state manager) translates the already-authoritative EntryProduceError into the appropriate ProducerEvent fields.

- ErrorCode
- Error
- CleanupRequired
- Producer
- Side
- OrderID
- DecisionID
- Stage

