13. DORMANCY SUPPORT
==================================================

Add support for:

"Which producer hasn't fired in two weeks and why?"

The 24-hour Producer Monitor state alone cannot prove two-week dormancy, so preserve or add a lightweight longer-lived per-producer observation needed for this question.

At minimum retain:

- last produced time for every producer
- last evaluation/rejection/blocker information if the existing strategy exposes it
- stable blocker/rejection reason counts where available

Do not claim why a producer has not fired unless the code has actual blocker/evaluation evidence.

If the system only knows the last produced time, report that and explicitly state that no blocker evidence is available.

Do not use absence of a produced event alone as proof of a specific failure.

This dormancy support must be additive and must not interfere with the 24-hour attempt map.

